# Adding an attack and setter to move

# resources
- 24+ players
- 10+ balls
- 2 coaches
- 1hour 30 mins
- 2 courts

# Focus 
Adding a chance to attack into our session and making a setter / defender move to the ball in play

# Warmup
- Normal warmup
  Rotating in 3's starting with a throw

  Adding a serve to the partner

  Adding an attack to the partner (hit down to the floor)

# Activity 1 - Attack and catch
Using a dodgeball

- 3 vs 3 half court
- Cones setup at half way into the court inside (closer to the net) is out
- Can add a jump and an approach and can throw from anywhere
- If you catch you win the point, otherwise the attacker wins
- Taking it in turns

# Activity 2 - 2 vs 2 Serve and Serve receive
- In 2's playing from a side serving in
  - Can use any serve we have tried, I.E an overhand, or underhand
- A pass and an attack / play over the net
- Rotate round every 3 points, king / queen of the court style

# Activity 3 - 3 vs 3
- We introduce the setter at position 1
- They have to run around and in front of the defender, attempting a pass and an attack
- Explain that the setter cannot attack the ball when they're back court

# Activity 4 - Gameplay,
Can choose to go 6 vs 6 full court or 3 vs 3 on a half court
